  "releaseNotes": "0.6.0-preview.2: Apply-only aggregate governance is now hard-enforced — AGG001-004 promoted from Info to Error, so a public/internal aggregate mutator, public setter, parameterized constructor, or object-initializer state assignment fails the build (in-IDE and CI). Consumers that cleared their violations under preview.1 (Info) stay green. Also fixes an AGG001 over-report on object initializers (now AGG004 only) and stops flagging the abstract framework bases (AggregateRoot/OrganizationAggregateRoot). See CHANGELOG.md.",
